---
import MainLayout from '@/layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import '@/styles/legal-pages.css';
---

<MainLayout title="Terms of Service | Kersivo">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="container legal-page__inner">
      <h1 class="legal-page__title">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: 9 April 2026</p>

      <p>
        These Terms govern the provision of barbershop website, booking, and retail pickup software and related services
        offered under the Kersivo name. They are intended for business customers (barbershops) in the UK. They do not
        constitute legal advice; have them reviewed for your situation.
      </p>

      <h2>Parties</h2>
      <div class="legal-placeholder">
        [TO BE COMPLETED: legal name of the service provider, address, registration details]
      </div>
      <p>
        <strong>Client</strong> means the barbershop or business that orders the work. By using the service after we
        confirm your order or give you access, you agree to these Terms.
      </p>

      <h2>What we provide</h2>
      <p>Depending on the package you choose, services may include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>a bespoke or brief-led marketing website;</li>
        <li>integrated online booking on your domain;</li>
        <li>an admin panel for team, diary, retail, and reports;</li>
        <li>buy-and-collect retail with checkout through Stripe on <strong>your</strong> Stripe account;</li>
        <li>ongoing hosting and support where you subscribe to Ongoing Care.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Feature lists and fees on our pricing page form part of these Terms by reference. Kersivo does not charge
        commission on bookings or shop sales; card processing fees are charged by Stripe under your agreement with
        Stripe.
      </p>

      <h2>Fees and payment (build)</h2>
      <p>
        Build fees are as quoted (for example Essential or PRO totals shown on our site). Unless otherwise agreed in
        writing, payment is <strong>50% to start</strong> and <strong>50% before go-live</strong>. You will have a
        reasonable opportunity to review before the final payment and request a small round of final tweaks as
        described in our FAQ.
      </p>

      <h2>Ongoing Care</h2>
      <p>
        Ongoing hosting, admin, shop access, security maintenance, platform updates (performance and scalability as your
        shop grows), and related services are billed at <strong>£39/month</strong> Ongoing Care, unless we agree a
        different rate in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>If Ongoing Care is not active</h2>
      <p>
        If you do not subscribe to Ongoing Care after your included period, <strong>our admin panel and integrated shop
        are switched off</strong>. We typically help you move client bookings to a third-party scheduling flow, for
        example <strong>Booksy or another tool you choose</strong>. The built-in shop remains off until Ongoing Care is
        active. There is no self-serve way to keep our admin or integrated shop without Ongoing Care.
      </p>

      <h2>Domain name</h2>
      <p>
        Domain registration for the <strong>first year</strong> is included in Essential and PRO; you do not pay us an
        extra domain fee for that initial registration as part of those packages. If you are <strong>not</strong> on
        Ongoing Care, <strong>renewal after the first 12 months</strong> is your responsibility: you pay the
        registrar&rsquo;s renewal fee directly (or through the agreed billing path). We are not liable for loss of a
        domain if renewal is not completed.
      </p>

      <h2>Stripe and retail</h2>
      <p>
        Online card payments use <strong>your Stripe account</strong>. You are responsible for complying with Stripe&rsquo;s
        terms, for accurate pricing and product descriptions, and for your own tax and legal obligations as seller.
        Pickup-only fulfilment and returns policies are set and operated by you unless we agree otherwise in writing.
      </p>

      <h2>Your content and intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        You retain ownership of your branding, text, images and other materials you supply. You grant us a licence to
        use them to deliver the project and run the service. We retain rights in our own templates, code stack and
        know-how.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        You will not use the service for unlawful activity, to infringe others&rsquo; rights, or to transmit malware. You
        are responsible for the accuracy of opening hours, services, and product information shown to the public.
      </p>

      <h2>Availability and support</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the service reasonably available but do not guarantee uninterrupted access. Support response
        times for Ongoing Care clients are within one business day as described on our website.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, we are not liable for indirect or consequential loss, loss of
        profit, or loss of data, except where such exclusion is not allowed by law. Our total liability arising out of
        or relating to these Terms in any twelve-month period is limited to the fees you paid us for the service in that
        period, except for death, personal injury caused by negligence, fraud, or other liability that cannot be limited
        by law. Nothing in these Terms is intended to exclude or restrict any rights you may have under applicable UK law.
      </p>

      <h2>Force majeure</h2>
      <p>
        We are not liable for delay or failure caused by events outside our reasonable control (for example outages of
        major cloud providers, strikes, or natural disasters).
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the law of England and Wales. Any dispute arising out of or in connection with
        these Terms that cannot be resolved by negotiation will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the
        courts of England and Wales.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms. We will post the new version on this page and change the &ldquo;Last updated&rdquo;
        date. For active clients, material changes may also be communicated by email or through the admin where
        appropriate.
      </p>

      <p>
        <a href="/">Back to home</a>
        &nbsp;·&nbsp;
        <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
</MainLayout>
